d=json.load(open(p)); rows=[
('Q28','1. Animal categories are bird, herbivore, predator, primate, reptile, bear, and Petting Zoo animal. Bears and Petting Zoo animals count unless explicitly excluded.','“seven animal categories ... bird, herbivore, predator, primate, reptile, bear and Petting Zoo animal ... Include both special categories ... unless explicitly excluded.”'),
('Q29','1. Association II only; must perform at least one task this action; at most one donation. No worker needed. 2. Pay the smallest visible amount, cover with supply token, gain 1 conservation. Ladder 2,5,5,7,7,10,10, then repeatable 12; skip blocked spaces. On final space, pay 12 repeatedly and place no further tokens.','“Eligibility ... upgraded ... at least one ... task ... no worker ... one per ...”; “pay the smallest amount ... cover ... token ... 1 conservation”; “2, 5, 5, 7, 7, 10, 10 ... repeatable 12”; “every later donation costs 12 ... no further tokens.”'),
('Q30','1. Count upper-right Animal/Sponsor icons, plus water/rock requirements upper-left on Animal and unique-building Sponsor cards; partner continent and university research icons count. 2. Exclude left-side conditions and project icons; university reputation/hand-limit marks are not icons. 3. A card counts itself; doubles count twice. Card text overrides general rules.','“count their upper-right icons ... also count water/rock requirements”; “Partner zoos and universities ... continent and research”; “Do not count ... left-side ... or conservation-project icons”; “card counts its own ... Doubled icons count twice”; “Card text takes priority.”'),
('Q31','1. Count distinct adjacent terrain hexes; multiple touching edges to one hex count once. 2. A larger water area counts only hexes actually adjacent. 3. Connected regions do not change this; tile illustrations are not terrain spaces or requirements.','“Count distinct adjacent hexes”; “multiple edges ... one water hex ... only one”; “larger water area counts only ... actually adjacent”; “Water/rock illustrations on tiles provide neither terrain spaces nor requirements.”'),
('Q32','1. Playing a new Release into the Wild project grants 1 reputation; supporting a project already in play grants no such play bonus. 2. All Breeding Program cards have same requirement at all three reward spaces; choose any available reward space.','“Playing a new Release ... grants 1 reputation; supporting one already in play does not”; “ALL Breeding Program ... requirement is the same at all three ... Choose any available reward space.”'),
('Q33','1. In X:Y, X is condition and Y reward. 2. No-number condition or “per” pays once per fulfillment. 3. Numbered threshold pays once; with multiple thresholds use highest met.','“X on the left is the condition and Y ... reward”; “without a number (or with ‘per’) pays once per fulfillment”; “numbered threshold pays only once ... use the highest one met.”'),
('Q34','1. Connected: uncovered and shares edge with covered space. 2. Isolated: no adjacent covered space. 3. Border: lacks neighboring map hex on at least one of six sides. 4. Your zoo includes played cards, map, personal supply; any zoo means all players’ corresponding areas.','“A connected space is uncovered and shares an edge”; “isolated ... no adjacent covered”; “border ... lacks ... at least one ... six sides”; “‘Your zoo’ includes ... ‘any zoo’ includes these for all players.”'),
('Q35','1. Unique building must be placed when playing Sponsor; if impossible card cannot be played. 2. Use matching tile colored face up; rotate freely, do not flip. 3. Ordinary placement/terrain rules apply; no size construction payment. 4. Not enclosures; cannot house animals or count as terrain.','“must be placed when playing their Sponsor: if placement is impossible, the card cannot be played”; “matching tile, colored face up; rotate ... but do not flip”; “ordinary placement ... terrain ... no size-based ... payment”; “not enclosures ... cannot house ... never count as water or rock.”'),
('Q36','1. Both granted actions wait until Animals action and card movement finish. 2. Use granted card normally, then move it to slot 1. 3. Named Action cannot be replaced with X-token alternative; Determination (Any Action) may choose any action including X-token.','“finish the Animals action ... before taking either”; “use ... Action card normally, then move ... slot 1”; “Named Action ... cannot replace ... X-token”; “Determination ... choose any action, including ... alternative.”'),
('Q37','1. Search unused face-down base-project deck; add chosen/named project to hand and return deck. 2. Dominance does nothing if named project already in play. 3. Later play and immediately support through Association above board, not setup base row.','“search the unused face-down base-project deck”; “Dominance has no effect if ... already in play”; “Later play and immediately support ... placing it above the board; it does not join ... base row below.”'),
('Q38','1. Resolve after Animals and moving Animals card. 2. Clever moves chosen card to slot 1; cards formerly left shift right. Boost puts named card in slot 1 or 5; to 5 shifts cards formerly to its right left.','“execute after finishing Animals and moving that card”; “Clever puts ... slot 1; cards formerly to its left shift right”; “Boost ... slot 1 or 5; moving to 5 shifts cards formerly to its right left.”'),
('Q39','1. All targets of Venom, Hypnosis, Pilfering 1/2, Constriction need at least 5 appeal, tested separately. 2. Playing animal appeal may be awarded before/after ability; normally its new appeal need not count. 3. Multiplayer may replace interactive abilities with printed solo alternative text.','“At least 5 appeal ... EVERY affected zoo”; “playing animal’s appeal may be awarded before or after its ability”; “replace interactive abilities with ... alternative text marked for solo ... does not require ... solo mode.”'),
('Q40','1. Constriction targets other qualifying zoos ahead on appeal and/or conservation: one track means one token on target’s slot-5 card; both means tokens on its slot-4 and slot-5 cards. 2. Never stack two on one card; duplicates return. 3. Each loses 2 strength, including each multiplied execution; X can restore. 4. Return after acting or without effect at break.','“ahead on one track gives 1 token on its slot 5; ahead on both gives 2 ... slots 4 and 5”; “Never stack”; “loses two strength ... each execution”; “Return ... after acting, or without effect in the break.”'),
('Q41','1. At effective strength zero or below, use enough X-tokens to reach at least one, use alternative X-token action, or leave card until at least slot 3.','“At effective strength zero or below, use enough X-tokens to reach at least one, use the alternative X-token action, or leave the card until it is at least in slot 3.”'),
('Q42','1. Digging 2 permits up to two choices, decide again after each card between discard display card/refill or discard hand card/draw deck card. 2. Display card is replaced immediately, shifting higher folders down and drawing into folder 6.','“choose up to twice between discarding a display card and replenishing it, or discarding a hand card then drawing”; “decide again after each card”; “display ... replaced immediately, shifting higher folders down and drawing into folder 6.”'),
('Q43','1. Flock animal may avoid new enclosure if another zoo herbivore requires at least its size. Same herbivore can host any number. 2. Without host, house normally; later non-flock cannot join. 3. Releasing flock animal frees enclosure under release/fallback rule even if shared; no historical proof required.','“if another herbivore ... requires at least ... size, need not flip”; “same ... can host any number”; “later non-flock ... cannot join”; “Releasing ... frees ... even if ... shared. Exact historical residents are not tracked.”'),
('Q44','1. Activate lowest reserve worker to notepad for immediate use. 2. Take map conservation-point reward for hiring last worker. 3. If all active, ability has no effect.','“activate the lowest remaining reserve worker ... immediate use”; “Take any conservation-point reward ... for hiring your last worker”; “If all workers are active, ... no effect.”'),
('Q45','1. If no revealed card is an Animal, discard all revealed cards.','“With no Animal among them, discard all.”'),
('Q46','1. Choose highest-appeal target; acting player chooses tied leader. If self-targeted, Hypnosis has no effect. 2. Copy slot 1, 2, or 3 using target card’s side; use your own X-tokens; move borrowed card to slot 1 normally. 3. Venom/Constriction on it affect you and are discarded after; its Multiplier cannot be used.','“choose ... highest appeal ... acting player chooses among ties”; “If your zoo is chosen, no effect”; “Copy only slot 1, 2 or 3”; “using its owner’s upgraded/unupgraded side”; “You may spend your own X-tokens”; “Venom and Constriction ... apply ... discarded afterward; ... Multiplier cannot be used”; “Move ... slot 1.”'),
('Q49','1. Place Multiplier on named action card; bonus tile allows any card including Animals. 2. Next use can execute twice at same base strength; X tokens apply only one execution. Additional Multiplier adds one execution each. 3. After-finishing effects wait until all executions; break after first waits until entire turn done. Used tokens return supply; unused removed at break.','“Place ... according to its source”; “Two executions ... twice in succession at same base strength”; “each X-token boosts only one execution”; “each additional token ... one execution”; “defer ... until all executions”; “break ... waits until entire turn”; “Return used ... unused ... next break.”'),
('Q50','1. Two Multiplier tokens permit up to three executions, not four. 2. Multiplied X-token alternative may take two X-tokens subject to cap; cannot mix one X-token action with one regular action.','“two tokens permit up to three actions, not four”; “may take two X-tokens ... but may not mix one X-token action with one regular action.”'),
('Q51','1. Peacocking permits Aviary before Build II, if none already and legal site. Other placement rules apply, including Build II for restricted spaces. 2. Posturing follows normal placement including kiosk spacing; place multiple buildings one by one.','“may place ... Aviary before upgrading Build”; “must not already have an Aviary ... legal site”; “Other placement restrictions ... including Build II”; “Posturing ... normal placement ... kiosk spacing; place multiple buildings one at a time.”'),
('Q52','1. First Petting Zoo animal gives 3 appeal, second 6, third 9. 2. One Petting Zoo holds at most three; these animals count as small.','“first grants 3 appeal, second 6, third 9”; “single Petting Zoo holds at most three”; “They count as small animals.”'),
('Q53','1. Acting player chooses target among tied leaders for both Pilfering 1 and each Pilfering 2 target. 2. Conservation target needs at least one conservation; if all zero that component has no effect, while highest-appeal part resolves independently. 3. If self selected, that selection has no effect.','“acting player chooses ... tied leaders”; “conservation target needs at least 1”; “If all ... zero ... no effect. Pilfering 2 still separately resolves ... highest-appeal”; “If your zoo is chosen ... no effect.”'),
('Q54','1. Target chooses five money or random hand-card draw; never Final Scoring cards. 2. With no hand cards give money; with under five money give a card. With neither, give all money including zero. 3. Resolve repeated pilferings sequentially; target may choose differently each time.','“target chooses to give five money or allow a random hand-card draw (never Final Scoring cards)”; “With no hand cards, give five money; with less than five money, give a card”; “With neither ... give all current money, including zero”; “Resolve repeated ... sequentially ... different choice each time.”'),
('Q55','1. Pouch cards have no function; on animal release discard them, but keep appeal earned. 2. Sunbathing sold cards go to discard pile.','“Tucked cards have no remaining function”; “If ... released, discard its tucked cards too, but retain the appeal”; “sold cards go to the discard pile.”'),
('Q56','1. Extra Final Scoring card obtained before 10-conservation milestone joins choices when discarding one. 2. At game end score every remaining Final Scoring card, each capped at 4 conservation.','“extra ... drawn before the 10-conservation milestone joins your choices when you discard one”; “At game end score every remaining ... each subject to its own four-point cap.”'),
('Q57','1. Shuffle discard pile face down, draw randomly, make stated selection, return pile face up. Scavenging 3 draws three, keeps one and discards others.','“shuffle the discard pile face down, draw randomly ... return ... face up”; “Scavenging 3 draws three random ... keeps one and discards the others.”'),
('Q58','1. Snapping takes exactly one display card regardless of reputation, no deck alternative. Sponsor Magnet takes display sponsors regardless of range; if none, nothing happens. Ordinary refill at turn end.','“Snapping ... exactly one display card regardless of reputation; drawing ... not an alternative”; “display sponsors need not be in reputation range; if no sponsor ... nothing”; “Ordinary end-of-turn display refill applies.”'),
('Q59','1. Place Venom on lowest-slot action cards, one per card; duplicates return. Using marked card removes token, avoids all fees that turn, including X action. 2. If no Venom removed and any remains, pay 2 money at turn end; if unable, undo turn and choose different action. 3. Unused tokens clear at next break without effect.','“lowest slots ... at most one per card”; “Using ... removes its token and avoids all ... fees”; “Pay two money at turn end only if ...”; “If you cannot, undo ...”; “next break clears unused tokens.”'),
('Q63','1. Immediate: 2/5/10 money for 1/2/3 universities. 2. Conservation project work strength becomes 4 rather than 5. 3. Final: 1 conservation for three universities.','“2/5/10 money for 1/2/3 universities”; “supporting ... requires strength 4 rather than 5”; “1 conservation for three universities.”'),
('Q66','1. Immediate: 2 appeal per previously supported project (count missing left-edge tokens). 2. Break income: 1 conservation.','“2 appeal per previously supported project (count tokens missing from the left map edge)”; “B: 1 conservation.”'),
('Q67','1. Count different continent and animal-category icon types together, each type once; exclude research; doubled/repeated copies do not add type. 2. Gain 1 conservation per two types, rounded down; each other player gets 2 money per conservation gained.','“Total your different continent and animal-category icon types ... research ... excluded”; “Count each type only once”; “1 conservation per two types, rounding down”; “Each other player gets 2 money per ... point.”'),
('Q68','1. On play: 1 appeal per research icon. 2. Whenever any player plays a research icon, owner gains 2 money. 3. Final: 1 conservation with five different animal categories.','“1 appeal per research icon”; “whenever any player plays ... you, the ... owner, gain 2 money”; “1 conservation with five different animal categories.”'),
('Q70','1. Immediate 1 appeal per Americas icon. 2. Each newly played Americas icon permits a free kiosk under normal placement/spacing. 3. Final 1 conservation with five or more kiosks.','“1 appeal per Americas icon”; “each ... icon played permits a free kiosk under normal placement and spacing rules”; “1 conservation with five or more kiosks.”'),
('Q72','1. Immediate 1 appeal per Australia icon. 2. For each Australia icon played, may tuck one hand card beneath Sponsor for 2 appeal; tucked cards have no function.','“1 appeal per Australia icon”; “per Australia icon played ... tuck one hand card ... for 2 appeal”; “tucked cards have no further function.”'),
('Q75','1. Take two supply player tokens onto Sponsor. 2. When supporting a base project below Association board, may return exactly one token as one icon; cannot spend both on same project; above-board cards from base deck do not qualify. 3. Final: 1 conservation with five project supports counted by missing map tokens.','“take two player tokens from your own supply ... on THIS Sponsor”; “supporting a base project below ... return exactly one”; “may not use both ... same”; “Base-origin cards played above ... do not qualify”; “1 conservation with five or more project supports.”'),
('Q77','1. Each Build action may add one extra copy of a building built in that same action without extra strength; pay normal cost and obey placement. 2. Only one extra total; special enclosure one-per-type remains. 3. Final 5 appeal with full map excluding water/rock.','“one extra copy ... without additional strength. Pay normal money”; “only one extra building ... special enclosures ... one-per-type”; “5 appeal with a full map except water/rock.”'),
('Q78','1. Immediate 2 money per water/rock icon. 2. May build over terrain and ignore animal/unique-building terrain requirements; printed icons still count. 3. Covered terrain stops counting for Hydrologist, Geologist, Architectural Zoo; terrain need not be covered for full map. 4. Final 2 appeal per water-rock pair, max 3 pairs/6 appeal.','“2 money per water/rock icon”; “cover water/rock spaces and ignore terrain requirements ... icons still count”; “Covered terrain stops counting”; “2 appeal per ... pair ... at most 3 pairs.”'),
('Q80','1. Triggered by each actual placement bonus on a border space. 2. For each, choose any uncovered placement bonus on map, not necessarily border; simultaneous copies may choose same or different. 3. Final when all building border spaces covered, excluding water/rock.','“Every actual placement bonus on a border space grants an additional choice of any uncovered placement bonus”; “Several ... copied bonuses can be same or different”; “all building border spaces ... exclude water/rock.”'),
('Q82','1. Immediate 1 X-token. 2. Each Release support gives +1 conservation. May repeatedly support same release project with different qualifying animals, at most one token per project per Association action; each token is separate support for other effects.','“I: 1 X-token”; “Each Release ... gives 1 additional conservation”; “repeatedly support ... different ... at most one token per project per ... action”; “Each token counts as a separate project support.”'),
('Q83','1. Immediate 1 X-token. 2. Immune to Venom, Constriction, Hypnosis, Pilfering; for Hypnosis/Pilfering ignore your counters and find next qualifying player. 3. Final 1 conservation with all five continents.','“I: 1 X-token. Immune to Venom, Constriction, Hypnosis and Pilfering”; “ignore your counters and find the next qualifying player”; “1 conservation with all five continents.”'),
('Q85','1. Permanently choose small or large; mark chosen box; reveal until matching animal found, keep it, discard others. 2. Cannot play opposite type. 3. Chosen small gain +2 appeal, chosen large +4; size 3 remains legal but no bonus.','“Choose small or large permanently ... Reveal ... until finding that type”; “You cannot play the opposite type”; “chosen small ... 2 extra ... large ... 4”; “Size-3 ... legal but gain no bonus.”'),
('Q86','1. Immediate 2 money per small animal. 2. An Animals action containing only small animals may play one extra small from hand with normal rules/cost. 3. Then may take one small display animal to hand regardless of range, even if declined extra play.','“2 money per small animal”; “only small animals ... play one additional small ... from hand”; “then add one small animal from display to hand regardless of reputation”; “may take ... even if declined.”'),
('Q90','1. Immediate 1 appeal per water icon. 2. Each newly covered space adjacent to water earns 1 money, even multiple spaces in one building; adjacent to multiple water hexes still pays once. 3. Final 1 conservation if all water hexes connected.','“1 appeal per water icon”; “each space newly covered adjacent to water gives 1 money”; “even if several ... one building”; “adjacent to several ... pays only once”; “1 conservation if all water hexes are connected.”'),
('Q95','1. Place unique building. 2. Each bird icon played draws two deck cards; keep one, discard other.','“Place the unique building”; “each bird icon played draws two deck cards; keep one, discard the other.”'),
('Q96','1. Place adjacent to water. 2. Each reptile icon played lets you sell up to two hand cards for 4 money each; discard sold cards.','“Place adjacent to water”; “each reptile icon played lets you sell up to two hand cards for 4 money each; discard sold cards.”'),
('Q98','1. Each predator icon played triggers Hunter with draws equal to your total predator icons. 2. A double predator card triggers two sequential Hunters, counting both new icons each time.','“each predator icon played uses Hunter with draws equal to your total predator icons”; “double-predator card triggers two sequential Hunters, counting both new icons each time.”'),
('Q99','1. Place building and three supply tokens on card. 2. Per herbivore icon played, may spend one token and pay money equal to hand Sponsor’s level to play it subject to conditions. 3. Its own icon may trigger when Stable played; three uses total.','“place ... three supply tokens”; “Per herbivore icon ... spend one token and pay money equal to a hand Sponsor’s level”; “observing ... conditions”; “own icon can trigger”; “Three uses total.”'),
('Q100','1. Immediate 1 reputation and 1 conservation. 2. Place building covering at least two border spaces. 3. Take one in-range display card or draw one deck card; simultaneous benefits any order.','“I: 1 reputation, 1 conservation”; “place its building covering at least two border spaces”; “take one in-range display card or draw one deck card”; “Resolve simultaneous benefits in your chosen order.”'),
('Q102','1. Place unique building on two border spaces; may be separate from existing buildings but other rules apply. 2. Later buildings may attach to it. 3. Break income 2 money per adjacent building except empty standard enclosure; kiosks may be adjacent and count Side Entrance for income. 4. Final 5 appeal for full map excluding water/rock.','“place ... on two border spaces. It may stand apart”; “later buildings may attach”; “2 money per adjacent building except empty standard”; “adjacent kiosks also count it”; “5 appeal with a full map excluding water/rock.”'),
('Q104','1. Immediate appeal per connected uncovered building border space, never terrain. 2. Final 1 conservation per six contiguous empty building spaces, evaluate groups separately. 3. Count restricted spaces even without Build II; exclude water/rock.','“connected uncovered building border space (never water/rock)”; “1 conservation per six contiguous empty building spaces”; “Evaluate each group separately”; “count restricted spaces ... exclude water/rock.”'),
('Q106','1. Immediate 2 money per different continent/category icon, excluding research. 2. Each category/continent newly introduced earns 1 appeal and 2 money; identical double icon grants novelty only once.','“2 money per different continent/animal-category icon (research does not count)”; “each ... newly introduced ... 1 appeal and 2 money”; “double of same new icon ... only once.”'),
('Q107','1. May place free size-5 standard enclosure. 2. When playing large animal, ignore one left-side condition, but not terrain. 3. Stacks with Research Institute to ignore two conditions.','“place a size-5 standard enclosure free”; “ignore one left-side condition”; “Terrain requirements cannot be ignored”; “Stacks with Research Institute to ignore two conditions.”'),
('Q112','1. Gain 1 conservation for each animal category where your zoo has more icons than player to your right. 2. If they have none, one of yours suffices. 3. Maximum 4 conservation.','“1 conservation per animal category ... more icons than the player to your right”; “If they have none ... one icon ... enough”; “maximum 4 conservation.”'),
('Q113','1. Only standard enclosure adjacent to tower hex qualifies, not merely another rock. 2. Housing there grants two appeal again after release/refill; special enclosures do not qualify. 3. Tower is not building for kiosk income.','“only to standard enclosures adjacent to the tower hex itself”; “Housing ... gives ... again after ... released”; “Special enclosures get no tower effect”; “tower is not a building for kiosk income.”'),
('Q114','1. Standard enclosure must touch Outdoor Area hex. It counts two spaces larger for all purposes after placement, including release/transfer. 2. No special-enclosure effect; Outdoor Area is not a building.','“standard enclosure touching the Outdoor Area hex”; “counts as two spaces larger for all purposes after placement”; “cannot be ignored on release or transfer”; “No effect on special enclosures”; “not a building.”'),
('Q115','1. Building on adjacent building space activates Harbor; first building may start beside it but need not. 2. Discard ability once per own turn before/during/after action, never breaks/opponents turn. 3. Harbor is not a building.','“building on its adjacent building space connects/activates it”; “first building may start beside ... but need not”; “once per own turn ... never during breaks or another player’s turn”; “Harbor is not a building.”'),
('Q116','1. Restaurant earns 1 money per adjacent covered hex, regardless type/occupancy; empty enclosures count and each hex counts. 2. Restaurant is not a building and gives no kiosk income. 3. Bonus is one free Reptile House OR one free Aviary, before Build II allowed, not both; other placement rules apply.','“one money per adjacent covered hex ... regardless ... Empty enclosures qualify; several ... each count”; “not a building and contributes zero income”; “gain one Reptile House or one Large Bird Aviary free ... Choose one, not both ... normal placement rules.”'),
('Q119','1. Cover H with buildings under normal rules; each reveals until Sponsor, keep it/discard others. 2. H is not placement bonus, no Archaeologist. 3. After all three, Sponsor level -1. 4. Bonus partners still need Association II for 3rd/4th; buildings need Build II for restricted spaces.','“cover H spaces ... ordinary placement”; “reveal ... until a Sponsor appears”; “H is not a placement bonus”; “After covering all three ... level one lower”; “bonus partner zoos still require Association II ... buildings ... Build II.”'),
('Q123','1. Pay money equal to Sponsor level; normal conditions apply. 2. Play only from hand, not display even with Sponsors II. 3. Sponsors card stays in current slot.','“costs money equal to ... level and requires ... conditions”; “Play it only from hand”; “leaves ... Sponsors Action card in its current slot; it does not move.”'),
('Q124','1. Appeal cannot exceed 113, conservation cannot exceed 41; gains beyond ends are lost.','“Appeal cannot exceed 113, nor conservation 41; gains beyond those ends are lost.”'),
('Q125','1. Venom: every other higher-appeal zoo meeting 5 appeal. Hypnosis: highest appeal >=5, choose tied leader, may target self with no effect; copy slot 1–3. Pilfering 1: highest appeal >=5, acting player breaks ties, self no effect. Pilfering 2 selects highest appeal and most conservation separately, each >=5; conservation target needs >=1; tied choices by actor, self selection no effect. 2. Constriction: each other >=5 appeal and ahead on either track; one track gets one token on slot 5, both gets tokens on slots 4 and 5.','“Venom ... every other ... higher appeal ... at least 5”; “Hypnosis ... highest ... acting player chooses among ties ... Copy only slot 1,2 or 3”; “Pilfering ... highest ... at least 5”; “Pilfering 2 ... separately ... each ... 5 ... conservation ... 1”; “Constriction ... every affected other zoo ... one track ... slot-5 ... both ... slots 4 and 5.”'),
('Q127','1. Animal partner condition requires partner from named continent; Sponsor partner condition allows any continent. 2. Red max-25 permits play only with appeal <=25; marker is reminder, not general cap. 3. Minimum reputation requires printed minimum. 4. −1 ignores one left-edge requirement only; all others and terrain remain.','“Animal partner-zoo condition ... from its continent; Sponsor ... any continent”; “maximum 25 ... at most 25 ... marker ... not a general track cap”; “minimum-reputation ... at least ... value”; “ignore one requirement ... all other ... terrain ... not waived.”'),
('Q133','1. Up to twice choose between discard display and replenish, or discard a hand card then draw one deck card. 2. Choose separately after each selection.','“Digging 2 ... choose up to twice between ... display ... or ... hand ... then drawing”; “decide again after each card which option.”'),
('Q134','1. For ordinary display refill after taking cards, move cards from higher folders down preserving their order, then fill empty spaces from deck. 2. During break discard folders 1 and 2, shift remaining down, refill display. The summary does not state an independent alternate order for moving/refilling beyond these steps.','“move cards from higher-numbered folders down (keeping their order), then fill empty spaces from the deck”; “discard the two bottom cards ... move remaining cards down, and refill.”'),
('Q137','1. Build standard enclosure empty side up, yellow border/size number. 2. Each covered placement bonus is gained immediately once; occupied later does not trigger it again.','“Place ... empty side up”; “Each placement-bonus icon covered is awarded immediately once”; “turning occupied later does not award ... again.”'),
('Q139','1. Discard one Final Scoring card face down under the remaining pile.','“choose and discard one ... (face down under the remaining pile).”'),
('Q140','1. Randomly determine start player; turns proceed clockwise, one at a time; no formal rounds. 2. Normally one action on your turn using one of five Action cards. Additional effects resolve as specified after/within that action.','“Randomly determine a start player. Turn order is clockwise”; “does not play in formal rounds”; “players simply take turns ...”; “On your turn you always perform one action using one ... 5 Action cards.”'),
('Q141','1. If nobody reaches 10 conservation before game ends, all players discard one Final Scoring card before end-game scoring begins. Destination/orientation beyond this are unsupported in the summary.','“If no one reaches 10 conservation points before the game ends, all players must discard one Final Scoring card before end-game scoring begins.”')]
for i,a,e in rows:d['answers'].append({'id':i,'answer':a,'support':'partial' if i=='Q134' or i=='Q141' else 'supported','evidence':e})
json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)
